  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing access of refugees to labour mobility pathways through skills development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to establish a pilot to address the barriers faced by refugees in Malaysia in accessing labor migration opportunities. This initiative will empower refugees by equipping them with the necessary skills required for migration pathways to a destination country (tentatively Australia). In collaboration with a local training centre in Malaysia, the project will provide demand-driven training aligned with labour market needs in industrial sectors abroad. In its initial phase, the project will gather data to understand existing barriers and identify opportunities for labour migration from Malaysia to target destination countries. The project aims to create a pilot labour mobility pathway with one country, which will serve as a model for future inclusion of other countries. The project will be implemented under the Malaysia-UN SDG Trust Fund as a joint program between IOM and UNIDO. As lead agency, IOM will drive coordination efforts and work closely with refugee communities in Malaysia to identify beneficiaries and support their access to migration pathways. UNIDO will focus on providing demand-driven skills development through a local pilot training centre, ensuring that training is aligned with the labour market needs of the destination.  By improving refugees&apos; employability and enhancing instituti</narrative>
  </description>
